WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:09.390
Bradyon Next, Luxon Next,
and a captured mecha will arrive soon.

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:10.400
Understood!

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.900
Valiancer units' landing preparations, complete!

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:13.610
Captain.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.370
Yeah, I know.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:26.920
Hina!

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.290
Are you okay?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:30.400
Are you hurt or anything?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.930
No. Thank you, Aoba.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:35.100
Aoba-kun, stay away from her.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:37.550
What are you doing?!

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:41.850
It's nice to meet you, Hina Ryazan.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.930
I'm Kuramitsu Gengo, commander of this ship.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.290
Let's you and I have a chat.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:51.250
We need to discuss whether we treat you as a defector, or as a prisoner of war.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.950
Spread your wings

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:03.580
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.870
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:12.250
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:21.510
That world you see before your eyes

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:27.100
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.570
The pain of loss isn't something

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:34.530
You want to get used to, and yet

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:39.490
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:46.460
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.290
Can't go back

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:49.710
Want to go home

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:53.050
The two of them back-to-back

00:01:53.050 --> 00:01:55.090
Break through

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:59.840
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.180
Like painting over a colorless world

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:05.890
Let this sympathy reach

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:12.150
Let's build the future that we envision

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.360
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:20.160
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.750
Apologies for being so rude after we just met.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.820
Not at all.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:32.380
From a military standpoint,
I think it was the proper response.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.630
I appreciate your understanding.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:38.270
Well then, I'll cut right to the chase.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.470
Which side will you choose?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.600
Will you join the Confederation as a defector?

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.730
Or will you remain here, as a prisoner of war,
in the hopes of returning to Zogilia someday?

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.020
Returning to Zogilia...

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:52.400
is not something I desire.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.320
So you wish to defect?

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.110
I do.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.230
Then here's another question.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:03:01.910
If your former comrades were to now find themselves at the other end of your gun...

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.990
would you be able to pull the trigger?

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:07.280
Kuramitsu-san!

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:13.290
Couplers like yourself are a rare
commodity among the Confederation.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:16.840
You can expect to be asked to work with the military.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.190
If that happens...

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:24.850
As much as I'd like to avoid such a situation,
you would be forced to choose who would live...

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.520
Us? Or your former comrades?

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.140
There's no reason to blindside her with questions like that!

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.440
Hina just got here—

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.860
It's important to recognize this situation for what it is.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.440
Right, Dio?

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:37.480
Yes, sir.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.400
But that doesn't mean you have to...

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:40.660
I don't know...

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:43.160
Whether I could shoot them or not...

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.700
Right now, I still don't...

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.910
But I...

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.370
I want to stay here.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:55.960
I don't have any memories of when I was little.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:04:00.380
Prior to being found in Zagreb 10 years ago,
I don't remember anything at all.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.380
What?

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:04.430
I want to know who I am.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.050
And I believe that Aoba holds the key to that, so...

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.310
That is why I want to be here...

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.400
To be with Aoba.

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.310
<i>So Hina didn't see that?</i>

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:22.030
<i>Memories of herself repeating
the same timeline over and over...</i>

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:28.160
So, you only want to be with him to figure out who you are?

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.630
W-Well, I...

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:31.910
I understand.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:38.090
I'll submit my proposal to the brass to have you assigned to us as an auxiliary Coupler.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.590
I would appreciate that very much!

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:42.730
Interrogation room.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.160
Is Commander Kuramitsu there?

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.050
What's the matter?

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:47.930
We just received word from Joint Command Headquarters...

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.920
There's been a coup d'état in Zogilia which has resulted in the establishment of a new government.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.690
What?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:02.610
With the founding of a new government,
we've been informed that the military will be reorganized.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.200
Here is the official document from Evgeni Kedar, Chairman of the Provisional Supreme Council.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.700
From now on, the entirety of the Zogilian military will be controlled by the Administration Bureau.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.540
Everyone in the National Defense Force will be

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:15.660
placed under the command of the
Administration Bureau's Protection Division.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.250
Huh?! What the hell?!

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.080
Tarjim!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.000
You object?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.340
Of course I do!

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:25.340
Then you will be stripped of your rank and punished for treason against the state.

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.220
Wha—?!

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:27.840
Please hold on.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.850
We've only just returned from combat in Alaska.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.600
It should be understandable that we find this situation upsetting.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.270
Though those at the top may change,

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:40.610
it is a soldier's duty to fight for their people and their country.

00:05:41.050 --> 00:05:43.820
Am I right, Commander Alfried Gallant?

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.070
Yes, sir.

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.570
Then here is your first order.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:51.080
You'll be headed out as soon as the preparations are complete.

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:53.920
This is...!

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:56.830
Oh?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.830
I had no idea you were capable of such a human expression...

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:02.840
Dr. Hahn.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:06.050
Bizon Gerafil...

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.970
I go by Evgeni Kedar now.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:17.230
What is it?

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:19.440
If you've got something to say, let's hear it.

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.190
Oh, no, forgive me.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.860
I see.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.690
So, you were pulled into that singularity and got sent back into the past.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.700
You catch on quick.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:34.620
Being a Coupling System engineer,
it wasn't hard to figure out.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.910
So? Is there something I can help you with?

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.960
Mister "Chairman of the Provisional Supreme Council"?

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.680
You already know what I want.

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.710
I'll give you all the space, funds and materials you want.

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.500
Build it,

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:53.220
your greatest masterpiece, and prove just how superior you are to the Confederation's engineers.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:54.970
Understood.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.980
Is this real?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.030
Yes, sir.

00:06:59.030 --> 00:07:03.190
These are the results of the analysis
I ran on the combat data from earlier.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:06.270
Next you'll see the simulation based on those results.

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:13.820
It's possible we've only been able to draw out a fraction of the potential that the Coupling System holds.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.700
How enthralling.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.960
Do you mean the Couplers?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.790
Or do you mean the results?

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:25.540
Both, of course.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:35.810
Hina.

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:36.720
Aoba.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.100
I'm so sorry...

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:41.600
I never thought they'd ask you things like that.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:44.650
I imagined it'd be a lot easier, so...

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.110
It's okay, it didn't bother me.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:50.030
Besides, you're a failure of a soldier, right?

00:07:55.490 --> 00:08:00.450
Hina, you said that you have no memories, but I saw them.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.460
What?

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:04.920
When I performed that Coupling with you...

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:09.510
You'd been repeating the same timeline over and over to protect me...

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:13.970
both as my classmate and as a Zogilian soldier.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:20.180
So I'm sure we'll eventually figure out who you are.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.100
When and where you were born...

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.940
What kind of girl you were...

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.480
It might be hard for you to believe that, but...

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.320
I've come this far by trusting you.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:34.570
So...

00:08:36.470 --> 00:08:38.550
I'll trust you.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:40.580
Thank you, Aoba.

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.580
Oh, well...

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.210
What are you doing?

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:53.550
I-I mean, it didn't seem like
the right time to interrupt...

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:54.720
This is work.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:58.930
Aoba.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.430
What is it?

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:01.890
Why are you both here?

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.120
They've determined where we're going next.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:07.560
Again? What the heck?
We never get any downtime.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:09.440
So? Where are we going next?

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.940
Huh? What?

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:19.240
Space.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.080
Several hours ago, we received this image from Joint Command Headquarters.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.840
As you can see, this is a Zogilian military satellite.

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:36.330
Not only that, but upon a detailed analysis of the image,

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:37.760
we now know that this satellite is

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:42.820
equipped with a massive Nectar Cannon four to five times the size of the one in Alaska.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.310
That much bigger than the one in Alaska?

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:49.440
Yeah. The one that blew away a few mountains.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:53.160
There has been no sign of any heat source, and based on our view of the exterior,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:56.580
the engineering staff believes that it's still incomplete.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:58.410
What's the expected time until completion?

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:00.620
Several weeks to several months.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.660
That's awfully broad.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.530
We aren't the ones building it, after all.

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:09.420
Having said that, we can't afford to ignore something like this.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:15.920
Left alone, we would never know when that high-powered Nectar Cannon might fire down on our heads.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:19.650
Not only that, but it can target almost any part of the Earth's surface.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:21.930
That they dared to make such a weapon a reality...

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:24.780
What is this thing supposed to be?
A thunderbolt from the heavens or something?

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:26.930
One that is convenient for the will of Zogilia.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:31.560
Therefore, this ship, and five others like it, have been ordered to mobilize.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:36.570
The mission objective is to destroy or disable the enemy's attack satellite.

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:38.650
Mobilize?

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.820
But can this ship even travel into space?

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:47.160
New ships like the Cygnus can be equipped with boosters to launch us out of the atmosphere.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.900
Using that, we can fly right on up.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:51.920
Wow...

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:55.880
But of course, the enemy is definitely preparing to intercept us.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.970
So with just six ships, it's going to be a little dicey.

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:05.390
For the purpose of this mission,
we are also to be assigned extra pilots and Valiancers.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.970
We will mobilize as soon as preparations are complete.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.890
All personnel are to get to work immediately.

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:11.140
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:12.280 --> 00:11:17.280
Or so she said, but it's not like we pilots have much to do.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:23.100
It looks like the maintenance crew is busy adding space combat modifications to the Valiancers, though.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.950
Just think of it as storing up our energy.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:27.790
Space, huh?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:30.210
E-Ensign Watase Aoba!

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.680
Pleased to meet you!

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.960
I am Ensign Mishima, assigned to this ship as as of today!

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:39.210
So you're one of the extra pilots the XO was talking about.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:39.760
I...

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.190
I admire you, Ensign Watase!

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:44.190
As both a fellow Japanese and a Coupler!

00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.720
Even though you said some weird things about coming from 70 years ago,

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:49.350
you managed to shoot down an enemy craft on your first sortie with no training!

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.690
Your combat record since then has also been spectacular!

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:55.360
I am thrilled to be aboard the same ship as you, Ensign Watase!

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:58.650
Y-Yeah? Nice to be serving with you.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:03.410
Yes!

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.570
I look forward to serving with you as well, Senpai!

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:07.870
Get a move on, Ensign Mishima!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:10.910
Well, then, please excuse me!

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:13.500
Senpai!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.730
He called you "Senpai"!

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:17.100
What's so funny?

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:20.510
You, there! No sighing!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:30.060
All engines at maximum power.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.070
Igniting boosters in three... two...

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.070
one...

00:12:55.910 --> 00:12:57.710
Detaching boosters.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.840
Contact restored with all ships.

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.160
We've reached the designated altitude.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:22.690
Maintaining safe navigational distance.

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.110
Looks like we've cleared the first stage without mishap.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.810
Awesome! We're really in space!

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.670
Come on, try it out, Dio!

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.000
Quit playing around. Can't you be serious for once in your life?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:43.170
A little bit won't hurt, right?

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.800
Multiple heat signatures! Missiles!

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:48.720
Deploy Nectar Curtain!

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:55.770
We anticipated they'd be here, but...

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.020
I never imagined such a swift welcome party.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:03.360
I may not agree with this,
but as a soldier it is my duty to obey orders.

00:14:03.360 --> 00:14:05.110
All units, open fire!

00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.320
I know you've been told this already,

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.030
but the space combat modifications made to

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.870
your units will put extra load on some of the Coupling System's resources.

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:16.570
Functions such as countering space radiation and providing balance in zero-G strain the system.

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:19.920
So you won't be able to conduct Couplings that go over the time limit like before.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:20.790
Just keep that in mind.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:21.790
Roger.

00:14:22.150 --> 00:14:24.130
Bradyon Next, taking off!

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.630
Luxon Next, taking off!

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:33.350
I'm a Coupler, too...

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.720
If only I had a Coupling Machine...

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.680
Quit your grumbling.

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:41.690
If we make it safely back to Earth, I'll introduce you to some girls.

00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:44.190
Girls that you're acquainted with, huh?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.440
There's no time for idle chitchat!

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.490
Lee Conrad, Beryl Commander, taking off!

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.180
Starboard side has been hit! Minimal damage!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.510
This is news to me...

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:16.600
Nectar Rifles that can fire continuously?

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.400
What the heck is up with those moves?

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:24.810
You've got "amateur" written all over you!

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.320
Don't come onto the battlefield with skills like that!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.410
Damn, they're here.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:37.550
Commander.

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:39.660
Yes, I know.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:40.830
You okay?

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:41.670
Yes.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.710
Stay back. Leave this...

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.960
H-Huh?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.000
What the hell?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.210
Th-They're...

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.550
The enemy is retreating?

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:53.590
Yes, sir.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:58.600
The enemy fleet, along with all their Valiancers, are breaking away from the combat zone.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:00.280
What's going on?

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:00.930
Captain.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.890
They're buying time.

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:04.120
What?

00:16:04.120 --> 00:16:07.190
There's no need for the enemy to force themselves to engage us.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:09.990
As long as they get the Gorgon completed,

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:15.280
all they have to do is turn the turret towards the surface and tell us, "Don't shoot"!

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.120
Then...

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.000
They've done exactly what we didn't want them to do.

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:23.700
If they attacked us, we could've found some opening to take advantage of.

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:27.250
But we have no supply line, and can't expect reinforcements.

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.960
Their strategy anticipates those things.

00:16:29.410 --> 00:16:30.800
What should we do?

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.720
We can't just sit on our hands and do nothing.

00:16:33.720 --> 00:16:35.930
We'll do as much as we possibly can with what we've got.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.680
Here is our plan of attack.

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:42.930
The Valiancer Team will follow behind you two and the fleet will provide cover fire.

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:43.940
Got it.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:49.070
Luxon Next and Bradyon Next are to create confusion among the enemy ranks.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:51.570
Also, they are to try and spread out the battle line as much as possible.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:54.320
Beyond that, we will look for a way in from this end.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:55.990
Roger that.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.950
Oh, could I talk to you for a second?

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.450
The new enemy Valiancers are coming.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:04.660
Right on schedule.

00:17:08.050 --> 00:17:09.460
Now, then...

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.800
Don't disappoint me, Commander.

00:17:13.300 --> 00:17:14.260
Here we go!

00:17:14.590 --> 00:17:15.930
Connect with Dio!

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.140
Accept.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:20.640
Deploy the mines.

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.020
We're already used to this!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:34.900
Mines won't stop us anymore!

00:17:47.250 --> 00:17:49.100
They've cut a path to the enemy!

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:50.130
We're going in, too!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.600
<i>All right!</i>
<i>Roger.</i>

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.010
Certainly, with your experience, I imagine you'd be able to handle things as they are right now.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:56.930
But...

00:17:57.290 --> 00:17:58.930
Bogeys approaching from behind!

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.170
I count 40!

00:18:00.170 --> 00:18:01.930
They're Zogilian Valiancers!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:02.930
What?!

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:17.030
So, they were hiding in abandoned space facilities.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.990
Could this have all been one big trap?

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:21.700
Damn, those smartasses!

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:22.790
The Cygnus!

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:23.410
Wait!

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:27.160
If we turn back now, the Valiancer Team that just charged in will be in danger.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.040
But...

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:31.130
We have to keep engaging the enemy and retreat slowly.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:31.920
That's our only choice!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.630
The Cygnus might get shot down while we're doing that!

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.170
You think l don't know that?!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.840
One minute until the Coupling time limit runs out!

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:42.180
At this rate...

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:47.600
Even you can't do anything about the passage of time, can you?

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:01.030
The time limit is up!

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.780
The Luxon Next and the Bradyon Next are Decoupling!

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:05.990
Damn it!

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:09.580
What?!

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:10.500
What's that?

00:19:12.750 --> 00:19:13.840
It can't be!

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:14.880
Fire!

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:24.220
Aoba!

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:57.550
Are you all right, Aoba?!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.760
Yeah, you saved me.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:00.720
But...

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.680
Damn it!

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.470
The Goshawk and the Kestrel have been destroyed!

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:10.060
No way...

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.020
The Gorgon was already complete?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:16.400
We've lost the signals from 73 Valiancers.

00:20:16.830 --> 00:20:19.700
Nearly half our forces in just one strike...

00:20:19.700 --> 00:20:20.990
That's not all.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:21.860
What?

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:25.030
They've hit Alaska Base.

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:31.870
This... this can't be happening.

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:35.500
We sacrificed our own men...

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.290
This is war.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.380
We destroyed more than half the enemy's forces.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:45.010
On top of that, we disposed of the Gala Puska,
Alaska Base and all, which had fallen into the Confederation's hands.

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.510
This is a great military achievement.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.260
Go.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:52.230
Annihilate the rest of the enemy!

00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:56.230
Enemy Valiancer team, incoming!

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:58.450
We have no choice now.

00:20:58.450 --> 00:21:00.730
The Gorgon has already been completed.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:05.490
We've also lost the option of counter-attacking by restoring the cannon at the Alaska Base.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:10.950
The only path left to us is to bring that thing down with our limited firepower.

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:13.660
We should fight, too, Aoba.

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:16.210
Hina, are you sure?
The people we're up against are...

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:19.670
I can't act like that weapon doesn't exist.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:21.460
There's no choice but to fight!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.460
I understand.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:23.720
All right, let's go!

00:21:27.590 --> 00:21:28.470
What was that?!

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:29.510
I don't know!

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:33.270
Some sort of interference is disturbing the Coupling System and...

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:38.770
This is...

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:41.190
They've been forcibly Decoupled?!

00:21:58.420 --> 00:21:59.670
Aoba!

00:22:01.170 --> 00:22:02.420
What's that?!

00:22:08.150 --> 00:22:10.720
Now, let's begin.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:15.910
I've been waiting 70 years for this moment!

00:22:17.130 --> 00:22:20.880
With my heart, I call out

00:22:20.880 --> 00:22:25.260
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:29.770
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:22:29.770 --> 00:22:34.400
Just for now, please

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:38.570
I know you

00:22:38.570 --> 00:22:43.070
I'm searching for you

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:45.530
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:45.530 --> 00:22:52.160
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:52.160 --> 00:23:00.710
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:23:00.710 --> 00:23:05.300
To the many gentle mornings...

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:09.850
and the times I have wondered

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:14.100
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:23:14.100 --> 00:23:16.350
I want to save you,

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:18.440
I want to protect you

00:23:18.440 --> 00:23:22.820
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:25.700
Wait for me

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:30.450
The love we'll surely find

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:35.250
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:37.640 --> 00:23:41.800
Next time: "Into the Skies of Tomorrow - Second Half."
